System Disruption Management, within the Global Operations Center, serves as the control point for disruptions across Waymo, orchestrating operations-driven cross-functional coordination to ensure rider safety, fleet resilience, and business performance remain uncompromised as we scale.

This role will report to the Head of System Disruption Management.

You will:

• Drive Global Operations Center (GOC) Readiness for Major Events: Own the operational readiness and preparation frameworks to ensure the GOC and cross-functional teams are fully prepared for a successful outcome during large-scale &amp; high-risk pre-planned events, globally. &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Deliver Executive Communications: Lead executive-level communications, delivering structured readiness briefings before major events and ensure clear updates are provided during active events (through our 24/7 teams). &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Establish GOC Preparedness &amp; Mitigation Actions: Develop, audit, and implement operational playbooks, risk mitigation plans, and other preventative actions to ensure GOC resilience during large-scale pre-planned events. &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Lead Internal Planning &amp; Municipal Liaison: Drive robust internal planning and coordination in heavy partnership with our Demand Operations teams and Market Leads to ensure event plans are robust, while simultaneously liaising with governmental organizations to secure seamless municipal coordination for major pre-planned events. &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Cultivate Municipal &amp; Public Sector Partnerships: Act as Waymo’s primary operational liaison to municipal departments of transportation, public transit authorities, event organizing committees, and public safety agencies to align autonomous fleet routing with city transit plans and community objectives. &nbsp; &nbsp;

• Drive Continuous Improvement &amp; Post-Event Retrospectives: Establish a formalized, post-event retrospective framework to analyze operations center performance metrics and execution; synthesize these insights into blameless retrospectives and action items to continuously mature internal playbooks, operational tooling, and municipal coordination models.

